# File: scripts/__tests__/omp-sdlc-ignore.test.mjs
#
# Generated from: specs/255-ignore-plugin-runtime-state-under-omp-sdlc/requirements.md
Feature: Ignore plugin runtime state under .omp/sdlc
  Host start-issue previously treated plugin runtime under .omp/sdlc/ as
  dirty_tree because onboard and upgrade never ignored that path.
  This was fixed by adding .omp/sdlc/ to the host gitignore and untracking
  already-indexed runtime with git rm --cached.

  # --- Bug Is Fixed ---

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Bug is fixed
    Given a host whose only porcelain would be untracked .omp/sdlc/ runtime
    When onboard or upgrade applies the managed ignore rule and /sdlc-execute starts an issue from the default branch
    Then .omp/sdlc/ is listed in the host .gitignore
    And that runtime does not fail dirty_tree
    And start can create or check out the issue branch

  # --- Related Behavior Still Works ---

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: Tracked runtime is untracked
    Given a host that already committed files under .omp/sdlc/
    When start or execute runs after the ignore rule exists
    Then those paths are removed from the index with git rm --cached
    And the working-tree files remain
    And they no longer count as dirt

  # --- Edge Case ---

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: No regression
    Given a host with dirty files outside .omp/sdlc/
    When start or execute evaluates the working tree off the issue branch
    Then the run still fails dirty_tree
    And it does not create or switch branches
